#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363851 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4feb6eca-9baf-537a-bd96-4e75951c9f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363853} {:answer/id #uuid "861fc691-bc44-5884-aa45-fe3dda66296d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "861fc691-bc44-5884-aa45-fe3dda66296d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363854} :answer-field/id #uuid "61833109-c1bc-500b-ac07-6456a7f484a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e37ea72-4527-59b0-9b76-eb7bab82018e" :question/math-academy-id "q-316602" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-8)\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 3=-40.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-40\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
